Mathless Compiler Output Exception
==================================

Version 1.0, 2026-09-02


0. What this is, in one sentence

   What `mlc` produces from your source is yours. Running the compiler does not
   put this project's licence terms on the files it writes for you.


1. Scope

   This exception applies to "Compiler Output": the files `mlc` generates from
   input you supply. Today that is

     - the native module (`.dll`),
     - the generated C header (`.h`),
     - the generated Delphi import unit (`.pas`),
     - the generated MSVC import library (`.lib`),
     - the intermediate Rust source `mlc` emits on the way to the module,

   together with any future generated artifact of the same kind.

   It applies whether or not the Compiler Output contains text copied verbatim
   from templates inside this project. It does, and substantially: a generated
   header is mostly our prose. In one measurement, `discount.h` was 39 lines, of
   which 1 came from the user's source and 38 from our templates; the Delphi unit
   was 19 lines, 1 and 18. That proportion is the reason this document exists.


